{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>הדפו</b> — two times in the Masorah without enmity: הדפו / כי ה' הרפו. And this is what we say: 'and Elohim caused it to come to his hand' — a parable to two men, one killed unintentionally and one killed intentionally. The Holy One, blessed be He, brings them to one inn. This one who killed unintentionally goes up a ladder and falls on this one who killed intentionally, and it turns out he killed him unintentionally and is liable to exile. And this is 'without enmity הדפו' — and he wants to brace himself and stand but cannot, כי ה' הרפו (for YHWH let him fall)."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The phrase 'והאלהים אנה לידו' quotes Exodus 21:13; the parable is a well-known rabbinic interpretation of that verse found in b. Makkot 10b. The closing reads the two Masorah occurrences as a narrative sequence: the victim pushed off the ladder (הדפו) and could not catch himself because YHWH caused him to fall (הרפו, from the same root, spelled with heh)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:50.738593973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}